  "producer": "Shoggoth, drafting the role matrix under Probitas",
  "reviewer": "an independent agent the decision-maker chose; its reports, naming the digests each reviewed, are in docs/kickoff/1368/evidence/review.json and the body of the pull request that adds this record. The selected option also set the merge condition: the delivery session merges once the required invariants check passes.",
  "audience": {
    "id": "public-address-level",
    "rule": "Findings drawn from public chain logs may be published, including in this repo, provided every prohibited claim stays out. Trade: a public credit dossier on an address that never asked for one can read as Wildcat vetting borrowers, which Probitas says Wildcat does not do."
  },
  "entity_name": {
    "id": "neutral-role-label",
    "rule": "The entity field is built from role and venue, for example 'Borrower of record, Wildcat market 0x...'. No organisation name taken from a market name, registry entry, ENS name or explorer label. An organisation name appears only when it declares the address, which makes that address declared."
  },
  "conclusions": {
    "id": "debtor-of-record-only",
    "rule": "Conclusion-bearing only where the venue's own log names the address as the account whose debt changed, and only for that address's own sourced events inside stated coverage. Every other role is recorded as context and feeds no conclusion."
  },
  "venue_id_convention": "A field's venue is the id used by the module its at path cites: Probitas venue ids under plugins/probitas, Tabularium adapter ids under plugins/tabularium. Euler V2 therefore appears as euler and as euler-v2.",
